This is an altered version of Echo's Z80 program.

prog-z80.bin is Echo 1.65 (github.com/sikthehedgehog/echo, commit e326c87,
built/prog-z80.bin) with one change: the PSG frequency table
(PSGFreqTable in src-z80/player/freq.z80, Z80 address $1200-$128F) holds
periods computed for the NTSC PSG clock (3579545 Hz) with A4 = 440 Hz,
rounded to the nearest value. Echo's original table plays PSG notes 8 to 14
cents sharp in its lowest octave and up to 119 cents sharp at the top, and
about 10 cents sharp of Echo's own FM notes. Everything outside the table is
byte-identical to the original.

Built with z80asm 1.8 from Echo's source with the table change applied; the
unchanged source assembles to the original built/prog-z80.bin byte for byte.
The change has been offered upstream.

